You can see from Germany, it's
Europe West, which makes sense.

00:33:32.830 --> 00:33:36.130
From Singapore, it's Asia
East, which makes sense.

00:33:36.130 --> 00:33:37.930
And from New York, it's US East.

00:33:37.930 --> 00:33:40.690
So yeah, this is
actually really working.

00:33:40.690 --> 00:33:42.229
And if you see this
on YouTube, it's

00:33:42.229 --> 00:33:44.770
not going to work, because I'm
going to turn the service off,

00:33:44.770 --> 00:33:45.920
so don't even try it.

00:33:45.920 --> 00:33:49.379
But it works and
it's really cool.

00:33:49.379 --> 00:33:51.670
So obviously here, we're
going to be in the West Coast.

00:33:51.670 --> 00:33:53.840
I can't fake my location.

00:33:53.840 --> 00:33:56.430
Google is pretty
smart about that.

00:33:56.430 --> 00:33:59.100
So we're just going to use
the West Coast buckets.

00:33:59.100 --> 00:34:03.330
So what I want to do is do this
thing called set up buckets.

00:34:06.622 --> 00:34:08.580
And it's going to fail,
fail, fail, fail, fail.

00:34:08.580 --> 00:34:08.820
Why?

00:34:08.820 --> 00:34:10.868
Because I already did it,
kind of because nothing

00:34:10.868 --> 00:34:13.409
would have actually launched if
I didn't have the config map.

00:34:13.409 --> 00:34:15.989
If you don't have a config
map and deployment depends

00:34:15.989 --> 00:34:17.639
on that config
map, it'll actually

00:34:17.639 --> 00:34:20.010
be pending until that
config map is deployed,

00:34:20.010 --> 00:34:22.239
which makes a lot of sense.

00:34:22.239 --> 00:34:23.880
What I did is I made
a different config

00:34:23.880 --> 00:34:27.719
map for every single
cluster with the same name.

00:34:27.719 --> 00:34:29.460
And then all it does--

00:34:29.460 --> 00:34:32.870
if we can switch
back to the slides.

