I keep picking up the wrong one.

00:34:34.710 --> 00:34:36.780
All it does is it
gives the bucket

00:34:36.780 --> 00:34:39.897
name for that region, right?

00:34:39.897 --> 00:34:42.480
But you can see everything's the
same except that actual value

00:34:42.480 --> 00:34:43.830
of the bucket name.

00:34:43.830 --> 00:34:47.120
So the first one would go
in a US East data center,

00:34:47.120 --> 00:34:50.320
so A-East, that's for
America-East, I guess.

00:34:50.320 --> 00:34:53.199
And A-West-- I'm not very
creative with names--

00:34:53.199 --> 00:34:56.400
is America-West.

00:34:56.400 --> 00:34:58.850
And if we can go back to--

00:34:58.850 --> 00:35:01.567
yep, thank you.

00:35:01.567 --> 00:35:03.150
If we go to our cloud
storage browser,

00:35:03.150 --> 00:35:07.514
you can see I have basically a
bucket for all of my regions.

00:35:07.514 --> 00:35:08.680
And I have this test bucket.

00:35:08.680 --> 00:35:10.554
So the test bucket is
a multi-regional bucket

00:35:10.554 --> 00:35:12.050
that I was using originally.

00:35:12.050 --> 00:35:16.110
You can see that the regions
are actually local to that data

00:35:16.110 --> 00:35:17.700
center, which is really cool.

00:35:17.700 --> 00:35:22.900
Versus the multi-regional
bucket is for that region.

00:35:22.900 --> 00:35:26.230
So if we go into
our US West bucket,

00:35:26.230 --> 00:35:29.030
you can see that
it's currently empty.

